At the next station, a lot of people get in.
The U-Bahn is suddenly quite full.
An older passenger stops next to me.
“Excuse me, is this seat free?” he asks.
“Yes, of course,” I say.
I move over a little.
So he can sit comfortably.
“Thank you very much,” says the man and smiles.
“Do you have to travel far?” I ask.
“No, I only have to travel to the center,” he says.
“With the U-Bahn, that is luckily fast.”
He looks to the window.
"The sun is shining nice and warm," he says.
"The weather is really nice today."
"Yes, spring is finally coming," I say.
"Hopefully it stays like this," he says.
“I hope so very much,” I answer.
